{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049128-idea-tomes-on-supernaturals","id":1049128,"title":"[Idea] Tomes on supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-14T21:12:31-08:00","id":1049128,"title":"[Idea] Tomes on supernaturals","content":"I <i>literally</i> just dreamed about it - Series of in-setting books describing supernatural phenomena in terms of <b>Mage</b> cosmology. I know it's probably looks like 'mage supersamcy', but Orders would surly do this. Thing like 'vampires are risen by Stygia emanation on corpse' or 'Primal Wild is in high of werewolves condition'. Things that Mysterium would surely write about, but would probably do not want it to spil outside as too embarrassing works. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T21:27:54-08:00","id":1049136,"title":"","content":"The types of examples you're giving aren't going to produce enough content to fill anything tome-sized, not least because the knowledge of the Arcana does not translate to jargon of its own. Conventional writings about Phenomenal monsters are necessarily going to look at the nature of their subjects in practical terms; anything that's not pure theory is going to amount to records of specimens and their proximate Supernal entities and other things Scrutiny turns up \u2014 related Mysteries being the biggest one.<br /> <br /> This is the kind of stuff that turns up in Advanced Libraries. There are cabals that form to collect this kind of data on single topics the world over. It's a lot of legwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T22:43:00-08:00","id":1049152,"title":"","content":"I doubt an in-character &quot;Encyclopedia Magica&quot;-type product is anywhere near a priority for OPP. There's already more than enough game aid material that would benefit from additional supplements, and every other gameline corebook and supplement already mostly mostly satisfies your desires, including the upcoming Crossover Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T22:59:59-08:00","id":1049157,"title":"","content":"I was not writing on the real world supplement - rather in game list of titles that you could find in Misterium and other Orders libraries. List with short description of content. Maybe I will make some examples later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:28:25-08:00","id":1049220,"title":"","content":"Something like this, perhaps?<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vampirism</b></span><br /> <br /> Like the common cold and influenza, this particular brand of semi-spiritual infection and the resultant preternatural predators have been walking unseen amidst us as long as humanity can remember, with each individual and &quot;clan&quot; having a hundred pseudo-evolutionary offshoots. Indeed, the sheer resilience of the Curse and the myriad forms it takes is a trademark property of the so-called Kindred.<br /> <br /> On a superficial look, it is painfully obvious that the walking dead who refuse to stay down resonate with Stygia. In fact, there is a similarity between how ghosts cling to their Anchors and how vampires fixate on remnants of their former human life. However, upon closely inspecting their abilities, they resonate more with Pandemonium instead, with their mind-warping powers and a nigh unbreakable sympathetic connection their blood confers. Stepping outside the Supernal for a bit, their insatiable hunger for blood betrays a hint of influence from the Lower Depths. While what that hypothetical Depth lacks would obviously be an aspect of the Life Arcanum, the Pit is not so easily classified and thus there remains a topic for future studies.<br /> <br /> In mortal society, vampires make full use of their longevity, powers that cloud the mind, and supernaturally enforced sympathies to infiltrate every nook and dominate the upper echelons. The prospective mage who wishes to influence a large Sleeper organization for any purpose should always take this into account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T06:29:12-08:00","id":1049268,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a>, strap only some working title on to this, and we have<i> exactly </i>what I envioned in the dream! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:18:35-08:00","id":1049551,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I tried to emulate the clinical and academic tone a stereotypical mage would have towards other supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> No working title for the whole, but here's another one for those still interested:<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Lycanthropy, Uratha</span></b><br /> <br /> Contrary to popular Sleeper belief, lycanthropy, the condition of becoming a werewolf, is not infected like vampirism. Or at least, the most common form of lycanthropes, the <i>Uratha</i>, are not. It seems that the Change is a sort of magical atavism hidden in humanity's genes, quite possible marking them as a sub-race of human. While it is possible to track down those of Uratha heritage, there are just as many spontaneous Changes, making it a daunting task to track who will one day wake up and join these race of hunters.<br /> <br /> As shapechangers who are part-flesh and part-ephemera, the Uratha are easily the closest Fallen manifestation of the Primal Wild in all its bloody glory. The signature ability of the werewolves are their highly flexible shapechanging ability, and a level of communion with the Shadow Realm and its inhabitants unheard of in other entities. They seem to hold the ecological position of apex predators and hunters within the Shadow, hunting down spirits for sustenance and acquiring abilities similar to ephemeral Numina and Influences from them. However, as with predators, sometimes the prey turns out to be too big to handle, and the smaller predators have no qualm about reversing the food chain.<br /> <br /> Werewolves in Sleeper society move in small units that may or may not include their kinfolk. They are highly territorial, defending members of their &quot;pack&quot; and the patch of Shadow they have taken hold of with simple but effective hunting tactics. Of note is how they often converge around ley lines and nodes, as the Resonance affects the Shadow just as much as it affects Mana. It is for this reason that claiming nodes and Hallows in unfamiliar grounds should be done in utmost caution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:24:51-08:00","id":1049557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049128-idea-tomes-on-supernaturals#post1049128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>literally</i> just dreamed about it - Series of in-setting books describing supernatural phenomena in terms of <b>Mage</b> cosmology. I know it's probably looks like 'mage supersamcy', but Orders would surly do this. Thing like 'vampires are risen by Stygia emanation on corpse' or 'Primal Wild is in high of werewolves condition'. Things that Mysterium would surely write about, but would probably do not want it to spil outside as too embarrassing works. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My guess would be that a lot of mage treatises on other supernatural entities would be along more narrow tangents. So while there might be something like &quot;A Speculation on Werebeasts &amp; The Primal Wild.&quot; it would be one of numerous works on various interactions and aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:45:39-08:00","id":1049615,"title":"","content":"And full of inaccuracies, especially considering regional examples. Cabals studying Montreal or Basra would get a drastically different view than one studying Thailand or Tokyo. The books are fairly open about that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T02:47:52-08:00","id":1049766,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is who actually writes these books. I mean, a mage researching vampires probably has lots of notes and information, but editing it together into a coherent book would a big task and I'm not sure a lot of mages would have the time or training for that. Either you end up with a lot of mage books being horribly edited and not terribly coherent or you get someone else (a sleepwalker or whatever) to do the editing with the understanding that the end product won't be precisely what the mage wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:04:49-08:00","id":1049830,"title":"","content":"How is this different from just Advanced Library?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T08:35:38-08:00","id":1049870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049128-idea-tomes-on-supernaturals?p=1049830#post1049830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this different from just Advanced Library?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These are in-character titles and summaries of the books that would be IN an Advanced Library.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> , Im really likeing these, keep them coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T16:49:48-08:00","id":1050150,"title":"","content":"I really wish I could amp up the verisimilitude on these excepts, by making them more narrower, subjective, and local. Like something a real in-universe mage would write up.<br /> <br /> Oh well. It's not like that those things ever stopped me, and I'm enjoying this at the moment.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Changelings and Goblins</span></b><br /> <br /> Of all the myriad forms of non-Supernal phenomena in the Fallen world, the Land of Faerie and its inhabitants are mostly agreed to be the hardest to define, for they lack any sense of commonality in their diverse manifestations. The clearest line of demarcation is in the fairies' place of origin, or at least, their self-proclaimed place of origin. Changelings are the humanoid fae who claim to have been abducted to the Land of Faerie, only to escape from it. Goblins are the non-humanoid fae who visit the mortal world through Irises to the Land of Faerie. However, even this categorization is suspect, as there are humanoid fae who never consider themselves abducted but still claim human origin anyway, and other humanoid fae who do not claim humanity at all.<br /> <br /> As expected of creatures associated with fairy tales, the destiny-symbols of Arcadia linger over the fae. In fact, some of the fae refer to their homeland as &quot;Arcadia,&quot; confirming that there might be something worthwhile studying in Faerieland. Meanwhile, traces of Pandemonic energies can be found in their emotion-eating qualities, power over dreams, and a worrisome degree of mental instability. However, the forte of the fae still lie in sealing spoken words into supernatural oaths and invoking certain fate-bound pledges to bend the natural world. The latter is surprising, since while it is obviously a work of the Fate Arcanum, the other party who should answer to the pledge is seemingly missing.<br /> <br /> Goblins, beyond their exotic qualities, are not much different from spirits and cryptids in their mannerisms, and can be dealt with accordingly. The real problem lies with the changelings. The precious few interviews secured from them reveal that they are in constant fear of a third group of fae, a sentiment shared with the more intelligent goblins. What society they maintain is in fact a large-scale ritual to fend them off, as they speak. While of those rituals are superstitions and a glorified make-believe play, the changelings take them seriously and will react if disturbed. It is best to leave them be and study them from afar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:23:42-08:00","id":1050209,"title":"","content":"<b>Hermit</b>, great write-up on Uratha. I would only have small point to make:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049128-idea-tomes-on-supernaturals?p=1049551#post1049551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrary to popular Sleeper belief, lycanthropy, the condition of becoming a werewolf, is not infected like vampirism. Or at least, the most common form of lycanthropes, the <i>Uratha</i>, are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>By rules you can 'get' Wolf-Blooded status when being under Lunacy. There was implied that 'being bitten by Uratha' can make this a bit more possible - so I would make more like:<br /> <br /> 'Contrary to popular Sleeper belief, lycanthropy, the condition of becoming a werewolf, is mostly not infected like vampirism ( but there are singular raports indicating otherwise ).'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:28:37-08:00","id":1050214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049128-idea-tomes-on-supernaturals?p=1050209#post1050209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hermit</b>, great write-up on Uratha. I would only have small point to make:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> By rules you can 'get' Wolf-Blooded status when being under Lunacy. There was implied that 'being bitten by Uratha' can make this a bit more possible - so I would make more like:<br /> <br /> 'Contrary to popular Sleeper belief, lycanthropy, the condition of becoming a werewolf, is mostly not infected like vampirism ( but there are singular raports indicating otherwise ).'</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage who wrote the report knows about Wolf-Blooded much less than he'd like to admit. The few &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; he saw were just normal blood relatives to werewolves, with a few of them manifesting strange Spirit or Life powers at occasion.<br /> <br /> And me, the guy who created the mage who wrote the report, is busy retconning his poor creation's mistakes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}